# Mercury Pitch native — build constants. Committed on purpose: nothing here
# is a secret, and every one of them has to be true of the binary rather than
# of whoever built it.

# Where the ONNX WASM runtime is loaded from.
#
# This was the fix for a bug that shipped silently: the app vendors the runtime
# into public/ort (scripts/sync-ort-assets.mjs) and then did not use it.
# `configurePitchEngineAssets` in src/main.tsx configured
# @irchiinnuss/pitch-engine, but nothing in the running graph imported that
# package -- the root `src/` tree, which `@` aliases to, carried its own fork
# and resolved the base from THIS variable.
#
# The fork is gone (the root tree runs the package now), so the main thread
# takes its base from that call in src/main.tsx and no longer needs this.
# It stays because a worker is its own module graph and reads it there --
# src/lib/pitch-engine-assets.ts hands it to the engine inside the separator
# worker -- and because unset, a native build fetches the runtime from a CDN
# on the first tap that starts the microphone, which is the one moment it
# must not need a network.
#
# LEADING SLASH, not `./`. The fetch happens inside a Web Worker whose script
# lives under /assets/, so a relative base would resolve to /assets/ort/ and
# quietly fail over to the CDN. Capacitor serves webDir at the origin root on
# both platforms, so /ort/ is correct there and in `vite preview`.
VITE_ONNX_WASM_BASE_URL=/ort/

# Google sign-in: the two OAuth client ids, and they are NOT interchangeable.
#
# PUBLIC BUILD CONSTANTS, committed on purpose. An OAuth client id is not a
# secret — it is printed in every authorisation URL, it ships inside the app
# binary by design, and Google's own docs say so. What protects the client is
# the bundle id plus the App Store signature (iOS) and the package name plus
# the signing SHA-1 (Android), neither of which anybody can copy out of this
# file. The client SECRET is a different string, belongs to the worker, and
# never appears here. These live in `.env` rather than `.env.local` because
# they have to be true of the BINARY: every build of this app, on any machine
# and in CI, must carry the same two ids or the worker refuses its tokens.
#
#   VITE_GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID   the "iOS" client, used by the Google SDK on
#                               that platform. Its REVERSED form is also the
#                               URL scheme in ios/App/App/Info.plist
#                               (CFBundleURLTypes -> item 0 ->
#                               CFBundleURLSchemes -> item 0); change one and
#                               the other has to change with it.
#   VITE_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID   the "Web application" client. Android's
#                               Credential Manager requires the WEB id —
#                               passing the Android one is the single most
#                               common cause of "[28444] Developer console is
#                               not set up correctly". It is also the audience
#                               the db-worker verifies every Google token
#                               against, so it must appear in that worker's
#                               GOOGLE_CLIENT_IDS.
#
# The Android OAuth client (package name + signing SHA-1) is registered in the
# Google Cloud console and is never pasted into this file or any other.
VITE_GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID=940402390643-ja2q9gkengndjdc3904j7ijli3hjoi33.apps.googleusercontent.com
VITE_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=940402390643-sb89ek7ocuoikqpd5llc6ike4fasccdl.apps.googleusercontent.com
